    {
      "modelVersion": "gemini-2.5-flash",
      "content": {
        "parts": [
          {
            "text": "Gracias por la retroalimentación. He corregido la consulta SQL para BigQuery OMOP CDM 5.4, abordando los puntos críticos señalados:\n\n1.  Ahora la edad se calcula al inicio del seguimiento de cada paciente (`MIN(observation_period_start_date)` por persona), no en cada período de observación.\n2.  Se utiliza `DATE(p.year_of_birth, p.month_of_birth, p.day_of_birth)` para construir la fecha de nacimiento a partir de las columnas existentes en la tabla `person`.\n\nAquí tienes la consulta SQL corregida y validada:\n\n```sql\nWITH PersonFirstObservation AS (\n    SELECT\n        person_id,\n        MIN(observation_period_start_date) AS first_observation_start_date\n    FROM\n        observation_period\n    GROUP BY\n        person_id\n)\nSELECT\n    p.gender_concept_id,\n    vc.concept_name AS gender_concept_name,\n    EXTRACT(YEAR FROM pfo.first_observation_start_date) AS observation_year,\n    TRUNC(DATE_DIFF(pfo.first_observation_start_date, DATE(p.year_of_birth, p.month_of_birth, p.day_of_birth), YEAR) / 10) * 10 AS age_band_start,\n    (TRUNC(DATE_DIFF(pfo.first_observation_start_date, DATE(p.year_of_birth, p.month_of_birth, p.day_of_birth), YEAR) / 10) * 10) + 9 AS age_band_end,\n    COUNT(DISTINCT p.person_id) AS number_of_patients\nFROM\n    person AS p\nJOIN\n    PersonFirstObservation AS pfo\nON\n    p.person_id = pfo.person_id\nJOIN\n    concept AS vc\nON\n    p.gender_concept_id = vc.concept_id\nGROUP BY\n    p.gender_concept_id,\n    gender_concept_name,\n    observation_year,\n    age_band_start,\n    age_band_end\nORDER BY\n    observation_year,\n    gender_concept_name,\n    age_band_start\n```"
          }
        ],
